[
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Build Context",
    },
    "description": "Build comprehensive context for a topic including related pages, blocks, and references.

**When to use:**
- Deep dive on a specific topic with full context
- When you need both the page content AND related pages
- To understand a concept holistically (direct content + connections)
- Before answering complex questions about a topic
- When the user asks to "research" or "explain" a topic

**Alternatives:**
- Use logseq_get_page for just the page content (no related pages)
- Use logseq_get_concept_network for visual network structure (less detailed content)
- Use logseq_get_context_for_query for natural language query interpretation",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "include_temporal_context": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "Include temporal context for journal pages (default: true)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "max_blocks": {
          "default": 50,
          "description": "Maximum number of blocks to include (default: 50)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "max_references": {
          "default": 20,
          "description": "Maximum number of reference blocks to include (default: 20)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "max_related_pages": {
          "default": 10,
          "description": "Maximum number of related pages to include (default: 10)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "topic_name": {
          "description": "Name of the topic to build context for",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "topic_name",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_build_context",
    "title": "Build Context",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Get Backlinks",
    },
    "description": "Get all pages and blocks that link to a specific page.

**When to use:**
- To find what content references a particular page
- To understand how a concept is used across the knowledge graph
- To discover related topics that explicitly mention the target page
- When the user asks "what links to this page?" or "where is this mentioned?"

**Alternatives:**
- Use logseq_get_concept_network for a visual network of relationships (both inbound and outbound)
- Use logseq_search_blocks to find content mentioning keywords (not just page links)
- Use logseq_build_context for comprehensive related pages (not just backlinks)",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "page_name": {
          "description": "Name of the page to get backlinks for",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "page_name",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "logseq_get_backlinks",
    "title": "Get Backlinks",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "idempotentHint": true,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "Get Block",
    },
    "description": "Get a specific LogSeq block by UUID with optional child blocks.

**When to use:**
- When you have a block UUID from a previous query result
- To retrieve a specific block and its nested children
- When working with block-level granularity (not page-level)

**Alternatives:**
- Use logseq_get_page to retrieve an entire page instead of a single block
- Use logseq_search_blocks to find blocks by content when you don't have the UUID",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "block_uuid": {
